      "content": "Flaky tests due to environmental factors are incredibly frustrating to debug. Start by systematically logging all relevant environmental variables *before* the test execution begins, perhaps using a script wrapper. Then, introduce randomization in your test setup, like retrying the failing tests a few times to see if the failure is always reproducible under the exact same conditions. This will help determine if the issue is truly environmental or if the test is just inherently unstable.",
