    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "logging the vars might help but we already have decent coverage on env vars. the weird part is the \"resource error\" seems totally random. sometimes it's a disk I/O spike, sometimes it's just a weird timeout that happens out of nowhere. it feels like something is just interfering with the runner in ways that don't leave a clear footprint. what else should i look at to see if there's some underlying contention or something messing with the process execution?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the errors seem transient and resource-related, investigate the underlying host or container where the tests are running. Monitor system-level metrics such as CPU load, memory pressure, and disk I/O latency on that runner node during test execution. Also, check Kubernetes or Docker logs for any ephemeral node eviction notices or resource throttling events that might be occurring outside your application's direct control. This can often pinpoint contention issues that manifest as random timeouts or I/O errors.",
      "source": "target",
